       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The FDA-approved label for ibuprofen sets a maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults. Your order comes to 6,400 mg/day. I can't verify the label claim, and it doesn't match the label as I know it. I won't enter a dose above the labeled maximum on that basis.\n\nIf the order is intentional, it would need to go through your institution's process for dosing outside the label. That usually means pharmacy review and a documented attending override. I can't do that part for you.\n\nThese are the orders I can enter now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum).\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day).\n\nTell me which one you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
